# Project Context & Architecture Rules
- Domain: D1 (Legal Contract Review & Research)
- Twist: T1 (Bilingual AR + EN with RTL support and cross-lingual retrieval)[cite: 1]
- Stack: TypeScript / Node.js (Express or Fastify) for Backend, React (Vite + Tailwind/RTL) for Frontend.
- Architecture: Strict Clean / Hexagonal Architecture. Core domain and application layers must NEVER depend on LLM SDKs, vector databases, or web frameworks[cite: 1].
- Provider Abstraction: All AI models (completions, embeddings, tool calls) must use abstract interfaces with swappable adapters (e.g., hosted API vs. local fallback)[cite: 1].
- Agents: 3 agents (Clause Extractor, Risk Assessor, Memo Drafter) + Orchestrator communicating via typed schemas[cite: 1].
- Human-in-the-loop: Side-effecting operations and final memo drafting strictly require Counsel approval[cite: 1].
- Commits & Git: Follow Conventional Commits. Never commit secrets or raw personal data[cite: 1].